h you can get started with the most  quickly um  i said like any eyes it's a super useful  task and it's been around for a long  time and it's really great  uh one of the limitations is that  everyone usually has a very different  sort of ner task  and so it if you do want something a  little bit custom it becomes  a little bit it takes a lot more effort  to get that system running  which is why currently there isn't this  uh  first-class support for ner in haystack  but with the pipelines you can define  nodes so like you can define a create  classifier you can create a reader  you can define a node which would be any  r  so you simply feed your data into this  node  and then you might use an nr system from  say  from farm or from hugging face  transformers  do any r and rejoin it back with data  and  um yeah so there's definitely like the  space in a haystack  to incorporate ner into this pipeline  um it just hasn't been a first-class  citizen for us yet  okay um  okay we have uh another question  so is there any future scope for  digital automation of annotation process  at haystack during fine tuning of  pre-trained model  uh language model for qa purpose  yeah um so it's been like we've learned  a lot about um the annotation process  and a lot of this also comes from  um other research out there um and there  are  annotation is is very costly it's very  time consuming  and um yeah  it's it's a tough task but there's  really nothing that beats it at the  moment  and so what we really look a lot into is  ways to  make this process more efficient  and um bring better performance to our  models quicker  so there are quite a few concepts which  actually have been really really  interesting to us which we've  drawn some inspiration from one of them  is this idea  of question rephrasing when an annotator  has been  writing questions for a whole day  they often will start using the same  structures over and over again  and it's hard to break out of that  pattern someti